      "message": "This test depends on:\n- Panic data implementation in EC\n- Calling `exit()` from test thread reboots the system.\n\n**I\u0027m not saying that this is bad** - it depends on what you expect from this test.\n\nIf you want a pure Zephyr way to determine if the system panicked expecteadly (or unexpecteadly) you can define `k_sys_fatal_error_handler()` function here, take a look at [this example](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/release-firmware/fpmcu-bloonchipper/ec/zephyr/test/fingerprint/drivers/fpc1025/src/fpc1025.c;l\u003d267-278;drc\u003de4e7fda84b119c6fc8af37c399e87fb2350e1863).",
