      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was looking at the [k_sys_fatal_error_handler](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/main/include/zephyr/fatal.h;l\u003d68?q\u003dsrc%2Fthird_party%2Fzephyr%2Fmain%20k_sys_fatal_error_handler\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch#:~:text\u003d67-,68,-69). It looks to me like a function that causes the system to panic based on a reason that you give it. Is my understanding correct? \nIn the [drivers.fpc1025.fpc1025](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/test/fingerprint/drivers/fpc1025/src/fpc1025.c;l\u003d267?q\u003dplatform%2Fec%20%20k_sys_fatal_error_handler\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch#:~:text\u003d266-,267,-268), I do not see where this function is called. You are just overriding the weakly declared function. Can you elaborate on how this function is being called?",
